<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sack of Rome (1527)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1527">1527</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cognac">War of the League of Cognac</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sack of Rome took place on 6 May 1527, when mutinous and unpaid troops of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, including German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landsknecht">Landsknechte</a> and Spanish soldiers, stormed the city during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cognac">War of the League of Cognac</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-vii">Pope Clement VII</a> took refuge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castel-santangelo">Castel Sant'Angelo</a> and later surrendered, while the soldiers looted and killed for months. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> the pope's weakness allowed the citizens to expel the Medici and restore the republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sack-of-rome-1527.jpg" alt="Sack of Rome (1527)" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Lingelbach · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sack_of_Rome_of_1527_by_Johannes_Lingelbach_17th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
